# Training-panel oracle ceilings — 2026-09-10

`EXACT_ORACLE_DIAGNOSTIC_NOT_LEARNED_ACHIEVEMENT`. No learner, training run, policy run, or loss-based inference was performed. The older 8-anchor coordination value and 20-anchor acceleration value are not reused, stacked, or compared with these values.

## Result

All pooled EE values are ratios of pooled sums, `sum(decoded bits) / sum(joules)`, not means of anchor-local ratios.

| construction | pooled bits (Tbit) | pooled joules | EE (Mbit/J) | served PHY | rate-target attained | relation used here |
|---|---:|---:|---:|---:|---:|---:|
| legal base | 1.121297 | 101679.495970 | 11.027760 | 960/1200 | 127/1200 | descriptive only |
| first-improvement incumbent at 10 s | 1.256375 | 94526.287166 | 13.291278 | 1036/1200 | 141/1200 | actual comparator |
| certified first-improvement fixed point | 1.255889 | 93511.944732 | 13.430253 | 1036/1200 | 147/1200 | acceleration numerator; coordination reference |
| certified best-improvement fixed point | 1.249936 | 93911.175144 | 13.309765 | 1036/1200 | 146/1200 | traversal-order reference |
| bounded joint selector from first fixed point | 1.267555 | 92580.086399 | 13.691444 | 1044/1200 | 149/1200 | coordination numerator |

The actual score to beat at 10 s is therefore **13.291278 Mbit/J**, with **1.256375 Tbit**, **94,526.287166 J**, **1,036/1,200 served PHY**, and **141/1,200 attaining the rate target**.

## Construction and estimand binding

| reported figure | reference construction | information class | estimand and numerator | panel | traversal/order |
|---|---|---|---|---|---|
| coordination ceiling | bounded joint catalogue reseeded from each anchor's certified first-improvement fixed point; denominator is that same fixed point | exact realised boundary 0 for selection; current anchor plus declared prior-step incumbent; no future boundary | committed pooled EE over 48 realised boundaries; numerator is saturated full-buffer successfully decoded forward-downlink information bits, with no demand cap | frozen exact-path prefix, 12 anchors | first fixed point: ascending user ID, declared legal-option order, first strict guarded `F` improvement in ordered batches of 16; joint catalogue in stable assignment order, batches of 32 |
| acceleration ceiling | certified first-improvement endpoint divided by the configuration actually held at 10 s | same exact realised boundary-0 `F`; the 48-boundary endpoint never feeds selection | same 48-boundary committed pooled EE and full-buffer decoded-bit numerator | same 12 anchors | same first-improvement traversal; only moves whose evaluation completed by the checkpoint are credited |
| traversal-order gap | first-improvement endpoint divided by best-improvement endpoint, both starting at the same base and using the same guard | same exact realised boundary-0 `F`, declared option order, and 16-row microbatch shape | same 48-boundary committed pooled EE and full-buffer decoded-bit numerator | same 12 anchors | first: first strict response; best: exact best strict response per user with stable configuration-ID tie-break |
| 10 s comparator score | configuration held by first-improvement at 10 s, pooled across anchors | same as acceleration row | absolute 48-boundary committed pooled EE; same numerator | same 12 anchors | same checkpoint-safe first-improvement traversal |

Here `F = decoded bits - eta_ref * joules`. The served-PHY count is the selection guard and a separately reported outcome. Rate-target attainment is also separately reported; neither is folded into the EE numerator. Base construction and validation occur before the search stopwatch; the stopwatch begins immediately before legal-option construction. Joint catalogue construction/scoring and every 48-boundary committed evaluation occur after unilateral timing.

## Verified by running code

- All 12 first-improvement and all 12 best-improvement terminal certificates are complete. Each final pass evaluated every declared legal unilateral alternative and found zero strict guarded-`F` improvements.
- The bounded joint catalogues contained 8,864 unique configurations in total and were exactly exhausted. The selected joint configuration strictly improved boundary-0 `F` over its seed on 4/12 anchors; the seed itself remained eligible.
- Peak RSS was **2.525 GiB** (2,710,806,528 bytes), below 5 GB. One Python process ran at niceness 15; all six recorded BLAS/OpenMP-related thread controls were `1`.
- The interpreter was `/home/sat/mcrl-leo-handover/.venv/bin/python`. The read-only handover tree and its virtual environment were not modified. All generated files are under this workspace.
- Exact corpus provenance passed for configuration ID and complete default/incumbent mappings on 12/12 anchors. The corpus's dense nominal source call and the singleton nominal provenance check were numerically close at `1e-10` on 0/12 anchors and had equal served counts on 1/12. This is a verified evaluator batch-schedule sensitivity, so corpus-stored dense metrics were not substituted for the oracle's fixed singleton/microbatch schedule.
- A discarded diagnostic selected on nominal `G = F + kappa*Phi`; it is preserved only as `.scratch/panelceil/panelceil-nominal-G-diagnostic.json` and supplies no reported number here. The reportable run selects on realised boundary-0 `F`, matching the standing oracle construction.

