## Inferred

- On this panel, traversal order moves the committed fixed-point EE by +0.905261%, while bounded coordination adds +1.944795% over the first-improvement reference. The ordering effect is therefore material but smaller than this panel's pooled coordination band; this does not transfer the older panels' relationship.
- The pooled coordination gain is heterogeneous: 9/12 anchor-local gains are nonpositive, and the pooled positive value is driven by the remaining anchors. It should be used as a panel-level ceiling, not as an every-anchor guarantee.
- A future learned result can be expressed against the acceleration ceiling only relative to the actual 10 s comparator (13.291278 Mbit/J), and against the coordination ceiling only relative to the certified first-improvement reference (13.430253 Mbit/J). The two percentages cannot be stacked.
- These are exact/oracle diagnostic opportunities under the stated information and catalogue bounds. They are not predictions of what a learner will achieve.

